message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Russell 3000 Statistical Arbitrage — Pairs Trading Research System"
abstract: >-
  A cointegration pairs-trading study of the Russell 3000 built to be falsified: point-in-time
  index membership from SEC N-PORT filings, same-industry pairs re-formed every six months,
  a two-state Kalman hedge ratio, next-day fills with a per-stock cost model, significance and
  power under non-normal autocorrelated returns, Gatev-distance and random-pair baselines, an
  evidence layer that explains the result trade by trade, a second strategy family
  (Avellaneda-Lee residual reversion) and a trial registry. The v33 design finds no detectable
  edge on 2023-2025, before or after costs: the cointegration it selects does not persist beyond
  chance, its in-sample edge vanishes out of sample, and its spreads behave like random walks;
  the second family agrees. A pre-registered test on 2026 data is sealed until its protocol is
  filed. Validated on synthetic markets with known answers.
